This is yet another... cruel, but educational death. 
" I'll never do it again. "

I was playing a tourist. I stepped on a polytrap and turned
into a water troll beneath the Minetown. Great, now killing is
so much easier... well, I managed to beat a pack of winter wolf
cubs to death. I was already satiated from trying to eat some
creatures for intrinsics (elves, maybe). Now, I'd like to get
cold resistance.

My logic circuits go wild.

"I am polymorphed into a water troll. If I 'die', I revert to my
normal form", I think to myself. "Therefore, I can risk eating
the winter wolf cubs and choking on food."

But that was not the case. I was wrong  and the game ended.
Luckily, the death occurred in early game and even created a bones
file, which, just like a new variation of an old method
of prematurely ending the quest for immortality, remains to
be found.

(The phrase "Another way to snatch humiliation from the jaws of heroism"
is borrowed from a certain adventure game by Mark Crowe
and Scott Murphy.)


